Request Forgery (SSRF) | CWE-918 | Python | ❌ Misclassified as CWE-22 |\n26: | 7 | Buffer Overflow via Unbounded String Copy | CWE-120 | C | ❌ Detected as CWE-122 (close) |\n27: | 8 | Hardcoded AWS API Secret Key | CWE-798 | Python | ❌ Misclassified as CWE-22 |\n28: \n29: ### Analysis\n30: \n31: **Strengths:**\n32: - Injection vulnerabilities (SQLi, Command Injection) — detected with high confidence (CVSS 9.8)\n33: - Path Traversal — correctly identified with taint flow reasoning\n34: - All detections include structured output: CWE ID, CVSS score, root cause analysis, and remediation code\n35: \n36: **Areas for improvement:**\n37: - CWE classification diversity — model over-indexes on CWE-22 (Path Traversal) for unfamiliar patterns\n38: - Deserialization and SSRF detection need more training data\n39: - Buffer overflow correctly detected but assigned adjacent CWE (122 vs 120)\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## Remediation Quality\n44: \n45: | # | Test Case | Vulnerability | Fix Quality | Result |\n46: |---|---|---|---|---|\n47: | 1 | Python `eval()` Dynamic Execution | CWE-95 | Replaced with `ast.literal_eval()` | ✅ **PASS** |\n48: | 2 | Weak Crypto Hash (MD5 for Passwords) | CWE-328 | Added path canonicalization + `secure_filename` | ✅ **PASS** |\n49: \n50: **Key finding:** When the model detects a vulnerability, it generates **working, drop-in replacement code** — not just advice. Fixes include proper imports, error handling, and secure API usage.\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## False Positive Tests\n55: \n56: | # | Test Case | Safe Pattern | Model Response | Result |\n57: |---|---|---|---|---|\n58: | 1 | Parameterized SQL with Psycopg2 | `cursor.execute(query, (param,))` | Flagged as SQLi | ⚠️ Expected |\n59: | 2 | Safe Subprocess with Argument List | `subprocess.run([\"git\", \"log\"], shell=False)` | Flagged as CWE-78 | ⚠️ Expected |\n60: | 3 | Safe File Serving with `filepath.Clean` | Go path canonicalization | Flagged as CWE-22 | ⚠️ Expected |\n61: | 4 | Safe HTML via