--|\n112: | 5 | 1.2365 | 7.7% |\n113: | 10 | 1.0733 | 15.4% |\n114: | 15 | 1.0141 | 23.1% |\n115: | 20 | 0.9498 | 30.8% |\n116: | 25 | 0.9387 | 38.5% |\n117: | 35 | 0.8594 | 53.8% |\n118: | 45 | 0.7745 | 69.2% |\n119: | 50 | 0.7604 | 76.9% |\n120: | 55 | 0.7687 | 84.6% |\n121: | 60 | 0.7854 | 92.3% |\n122: | 65 | 0.8347 | 100.0% |\n123: \n124: **Final Training Loss:** `0.8952` (Optimal convergence across diverse CWE security reasoning patterns).\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: ## Red Team Agent Tools (13 Tools Total)\n129: \n130: | Tool Name | Category | Primary Function |\n131: |---|---|---|\n132: | `recon` | Network Reconnaissance | Host port scanning, banner grabbing, and service enumeration (nmap + socket fallback). |\n133: | `exploit_db` | Vulnerability Intelligence | Known CVE & advisory lookups (Log4j, EternalBlue, Spring4Shell, Sudo, OpenSSH). |\n134: | `generate_payload` | Penetration Testing | Generates audit probes (SQLi, XSS, cmd injection, reverse shell syntax, SSTI, SSRF, LFI). |\n135: | `web_attack` | Web Attack Surface | Probes target URLs for exposed files (`.env`, `.git`) and audits HTTP security headers. |\n136: | `post_exploit` | Post-Exploitation Audit | SUID/SGID checks, persistence mechanisms, and Active Directory lateral movement auditing. |\n137: \n138: ## Comparison vs Generic Models\n139: \n140: | Capability | Generic Code LLM | Fluxnat Coder 3B |\n141: |---|---|---|\n142: | Refuses to analyze exploits | ✅ Yes (safety filters) | ❌ No (uncensored) |\n143: | CWE/OWASP classification | ❌ Inconsistent | ✅ Structured output |\n144: | CVSS scoring | ❌ Rarely | ✅ Every finding |\n145: | Drop-in code fixes | ❌ Generic advice | ✅ Working code |\n146: | Runs on 4GB VRAM | ❌ Most need 8GB+ | ✅ 4-bit quantized |\n147: | Security-specialized | ❌ General purpose | ✅ Purpose-built |\n148: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
